        <dataSetInformation>
            <common:UUID>d9fad792-5b9f-39d5-814e-d15fd9a767ac</common:UUID>
            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Cable, network cable, category 5, without plugs, at plant</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="57aded3d-4d3f-3d65-b03a-7392ab36aef2">electronics</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="296c829f-9160-371d-9441-529c080d79d5">devices</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">This dataset can be applied to describe the production of a typical network cable for computers. The total weight of 1 m of network cable is 0.036 kg (without the belonging plugs). The information for this dataset is based on weighing, measurements and analysis at EMPA Laboratories. In 2023, only production efforts data are updated. Furthermore, material and energy input are now represented by global inventory flows; UUID: d9fad792-5b9f-39d5-814e-d15fd9a767ac</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
        <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
            <referenceToReferenceFlow>1</referenceToReferenceFlow>
        </quantitativeReference>
        <time xmlns:olca="http://openlca.org/ilcd-extensions" olca:startDate="1672527600000" olca:endDate="1890774000000">
            <common:referenceYear>2023</common:referenceYear>
            <common:dataSetValidUntil>2029</common:dataSetValidUntil>
            <common:timeRepresentativenessDescription xml:lang="en">Unspecified</common:timeRepresentativenessDescription>
        </time>
        <geography>
            <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="GLO">
                <descriptionOfRestrictions xml:lang="en">The data describes a typical network cable for computers in 2006. The kind of cable is produced by international manufacturers and available all over the world. Therefore a global dataset is justifiable.</descriptionOfRestrictions>
            </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
        </geography>
        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">The manufacturing process is represented by wire drawing (of copper), plastic extrusion (for LDPE and PVC), tin coating.\n\n# Included processes\nDescribes the production of a typical network cable used with desktop or laptop computers. Calculated per 1 m of connector. Included are the materials copper, soft PVC, LDPE and tin (as coating) with their respective manufacturing processes. The infrastructure is calculated via the proxy "electronic component production plant". Further inventoried are the electricity for the assembly of the connector, the fuel oil, propane and water input, the disposal of plastic and rubber parts, the VOC and methanol emissions created during the processing, plus the road and rail transportation for input materials from the regional storage to the production site. The accumulated hazardous waste is also reported.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
